Z||000003||Fierowrecker||03-14-2001||11:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fotofrank:<BR><B>I'm planing some head work on my Duke. If I have the head milled how much can I have taken off. I feel about 0.10 is OK. How much differancs in HP and preformance will I get?<BR>I am also considering using roller rockers. What brand,Lift and will it work? The two mods an a port jub should deliver some improvement.I don't expect to be faster than a 2.8 but if I can keep up with a few I'll be happy. I presently get 104hp, with my G-Tech. The present mods are MSD6a, K&N filter Holley TBI and Input. Also have an MSD coil. What do you all think? <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Frank...<BR>  .10 inch is max, otherwise it is recommended you replace the head...<BR>    Better yet, go to a flat top piston. the head provides 9:1 compression with the dished pistons. 10 or 10.5 with flat top???<BR>Personally, I am dropping in a 3.8L Buick with mods...<BR>That should turn a head or two!!!<BR>||||reg||1
